menu "Petro protection (PETRO-5)"

    config PETRO_OVERTEMP_C
        int "Over-temperature trip on the NTC (C)"
        range 40 70
        default 55
        help
            The NTC (TH1, beside the relay) reading at which Petro trips, held for 2 s. The NTC
            under-reads the hot spots, so this is set from Gate 4's ratio
            (docs/testing/gate-4-load-thermal.md 5):
                limit = room + (70 - room) / ratio, room = 35 C.
            55 C (a ratio of 1.75) is provisional until Gate 4 has run. A trip can't be cleared
            while the NTC is within 5 C of this.

    config PETRO_ZX_SWITCHING
        bool "Switch the relay at the mains' zero crossings"
        default y
        help
            Time the relay's close and open to the BL0939's ZX output, allowing for the relay's
            operate and release times. Without ZX edges for 100 ms (no mains: on USB) it switches
            at once. Trips always switch at once.

    config PETRO_RELAY_OPERATE_US
        int "Relay operate time (us)"
        depends on PETRO_ZX_SWITCHING
        range 0 20000
        default 8000
        help
            From the coil energised to the contacts closed. HF115F: about 8 ms (the datasheet's
            maximum is 15 ms). Measure it at Gate 2 and set it here.

    config PETRO_RELAY_RELEASE_US
        int "Relay release time (us)"
        depends on PETRO_ZX_SWITCHING
        range 0 20000
        default 4000
        help
            From the coil de-energised to the contacts open. HF115F: about 4 ms, longer with a
            plain flyback diode. Measure it at Gate 2 and set it here.

endmenu
